Address intermittent launchpad availability.

Launchpad has recently been unreliable due to denial of service
attacks.

The kolla-toolbox and rabbitmq images on Debian enable the
rabbitmq-erlang PPA hosted on Launchpad
(ppa.launchpadcontent.net) to obtain Erlang 27. Debian Trixie now
ships erlang-base 1:27.3.4.1+dfsg-1+deb13u1 in the base archive,
which removes the Launchpad dependency for Debian builds entirely
on both amd64 and arm64.

For Ubuntu Noble on amd64, the RabbitMQ team publishes the same
packages at
``https://deb1.rabbitmq.com/rabbitmq-erlang/ubuntu/noble``, signed
by the same ``RabbitMQ Release Signing Key`` (key ID
``6B73A36E6026DFCA``) that the existing ``rabbitmq-server`` apt
repo already uses.

The RabbitMQ-hosted mirror only publishes amd64 Erlang packages
(per ``https://www.rabbitmq.com/docs/install-debian``), so
``ubuntu-aarch64`` builds keep using the Launchpad PPA via an
arch-specific override in ``kolla/template/repos.yaml``. The
``erlang-ppa`` keyring entry in ``base_apt_keys`` is therefore
retained -- it is still required to verify the Launchpad PPA on
``ubuntu-aarch64``.

Net effect: Debian builds (both arches) and Ubuntu amd64 builds
no longer touch Launchpad. Ubuntu arm64 builds remain dependent
on Launchpad until the RabbitMQ team publishes arm64 Erlang
builds.

Prompt: Upstream review pointed out that the rabbitmq.com
mirror is amd64-only and asked whether we need to special-case
by architecture. Update the patch to keep the Launchpad PPA as
an arm64 fallback for Ubuntu, while still dropping it for
Debian (both arches) and Ubuntu amd64.

